contentText:
Cardi B captures a milestone 30th top 10 hit on Billboard ’s Hot Rap Songs chart as “AH HA” debuts at No. 3 on the chart dated Aug. 15. With the start, the rapper extends her streak of posting at least one new top 10 on the list every year to a 10th consecutive year.

“AH HA” opens with 9.5 million official streams, 5.6 million in radio airplay audience impressions and 9,000 sales via physical CD purchases and digital downloads in the July 31-Aug. 6 tracking week, in the United States, according to Luminate. As a result, it begins at No. 3 on the Rap Streaming Songs chart and is the top-selling rap song of the week. On the airplay side, it bows at No. 29 on the audience-based R&B/Hip-Hop Airplay chart, at No. 34 on Rhythmic Airplay and at No. 40 on the plays-based Mainstream R&B/Hip-Hop Airplay recap.

